            <chunk name="Object" index="0">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">921cd4ab-78c2-4be8-a061-4eeb0458ed10</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">BREATHING MANIKIN (CO2 SPECIES)
OpenFOAM 12 multicomponentFluid, TRANSIENT.
Units: METERS.

*** ~10-15 MINUTES TO SOLVE ***
snappy has to resolve the manikin body, mouth
and vent as separate patches, then a 10 s
transient runs on top. Needs the UMF image.

Room 3 x 3 x 2.4 m, cell size 0.12 m.
Manikin at ground position (1.0, 1.5, 0),
facing +X (the component default), 1.75 m tall,
0.02 m mouth patch.
Vent (pressure outlet) at (3, 1.5, 2.2).
12 breaths/min, 40000 ppm exhaled, 400 ppm
ambient, 10 s duration.
All from TestIndoorSpeciesContainerE2E.

PROBES: the Manikin's own Mouth output moved
0.15 m along +X (the fixture's near-mouth probe),
merged with a far-corner reference at
(2.7, 2.7, 2.0).

Breathing is a PULSATING jet: the near probe
swings from ~20000 ppm on the exhale back to
ambient on the inhale. Judge the trace, never a
single sample.

NOT APPLICABLE: Indoor Inlet and Indoor Outlet
do not connect here. Indoor Species Case has no
inlet/outlet inputs - its only opening is Vent.

Write ships OFF.</item>
                  </items>
